# Architecture Rules

Browser-only turn-based sim. All app code under `src/`; `docs/` and `.cursor/` stay at repo root.

## Layers

| Layer    | Path            | Responsibility                         |
|----------|-----------------|----------------------------------------|
| Types    | `src/types/`    | Interfaces only, no logic              |
| Data     | `src/data/`     | Immutable JSON content                 |
| State    | `src/state/`    | Reactive `GameState` singleton         |
| Engine   | `src/engine/`   | All GameState mutations                |
| Services | `src/services/` | External I/O (LLM, database, …)        |
| UI       | `src/ui/`       | Rendering and input                    |

## Hard Rules

1. Vue components **never** mutate `GameState` directly
2. UI calls Engine through `src/engine/index.ts`; reads via `useGameState()` from `@state/useGameState`
3. Pinia stores hold **UI state only** (selection, layout, modals)
4. Static content stays in `src/data/*.json` — never copy wholesale into GameState
5. Services wrap external APIs; they do **not** mutate `GameState` — Engine applies results
6. Secrets in root `.env` (gitignored); client config uses `VITE_` prefix (e.g. `VITE_MISTRAL_API_KEY`)

## Engine

Group by domain: `src/engine/time/`, `src/engine/characters/`, etc. Prefer pure functions:

```typescript
export function advanceTurn(state: GameState): void {
  state.date = nextDate(state.date)
}
```

## Data Flow

Player input → UI calls `engineAction()` → Engine mutates `gameState` → Vue reactivity updates UI.
Services (e.g. LLM) are called from Engine; Engine writes results to state.

## Path Aliases

`@engine/*`, `@state/*`, `@ui/*`, `@data/*`, `@/types`, `@/services/*`
